      "title": "LOW's Q3 Earnings Call Lifts Sales Outlook and Cuts Margin View",
      "summary": "Lowe's lifted its fiscal 2026 sales forecast to $92.5 billion and expects 0.5% comparable sales growth, but lowered adjusted operating margin guidance to 11.5% due to higher fuel and freight costs and a shift toward lower-margin products. The company plans to reinvest tariff refunds in Q4 customer initiatives, while online sales grew 17.4% driven by higher traffic and improved fulfillment options.",
